     <p><M05C2-BOUNDARY status="spec/done">The configured resolver consumes admitted, source-bound B1/B2 definitions and immutable C1 metadata. Unsupported combinations refuse before returning mutation effects. Completeness is the existing solver's finite candidate search, never a fixed retry limit. Legacy DepSolver routes, ordinary manifest parsing, B3 opt-in profiles and C1 operational-error propagation remain intact; universal caller-route parity is separate C3 work. Counterexamples compare the entire selected graph and all derived effects, including provider contributions.</M05C2-BOUNDARY></p>
     <p><M05C2-ADMITTED-SURFACE status="spec/done">The configured Rust entry accepts fixed explicit incoming Vibe consumer requests, one configuration instance per package, and normalized definitions supplied by the admitting caller with exact C1 receipts. It preserves the full request rather than inferring edges from installed state. Default authorization retains that request and the full shown normalized definition as well as its source/content/definition receipt. Native candidate selection, multiple instances of one package, cross-package feature forwarding and non-registry dependency sources refuse. Conditional targets, requires_any and obsoletes also refuse on this entry because the incumbent graph projection does not retain their complete activation support. These refusals are explicit unsupported outcomes, not unsatisfiability claims or a substitute resolver. The ordinary resolver routes and B1/B2 standalone APIs retain their existing semantics.</M05C2-ADMITTED-SURFACE></p>
